Narrative ID: aa42e210a361571ff4d1fad892b75d15
Narrative: How can a device avoid futile access attempts while still selecting connectivity for best throughput?

Maximum answer sentences: 5

Each evidence sentence below has an evidence_id. Use those evidence_ids to indicate which sentences support each answer sentence.

Evidence:
[
  {
    "evidence_id": 0,
    "doc_id": "129069349",
    "text": "The UE implements the trained deep learning model to predict whether a better DL throughput can be obtained by enabling 5G NR dual connectivity based on the features, such as the measurable 4G/5G KPIs, at the current location."
  },
  {
    "evidence_id": 1,
    "doc_id": "129069349",
    "text": "OPTIMIZING DATA THROUGHPUT PERFORMANCE IN 5G NON-STANDALONE NETWORKS USING DEEP LEARNING Abstract A user equipment (UE) in a non-standalone (NSA) 5G network uses a deep learning model to predict whether a better downlink (DL) throughput can be obtained by enabling 5G new radio (NR) capability to optimize its DL data throughput performance."
  },
  {
    "evidence_id": 2,
    "doc_id": "129069349",
    "text": "Background Many mobile networks implement multiple radio access technology (RAT) connectivity, which allows cellular phones and other mobile user equipment (UE) to successively or concurrently connect to different radio access networks (RANs) or a single RAN employing multiple RATs."
  },
  {
    "evidence_id": 3,
    "doc_id": "122371639",
    "text": "Obtain Inference Result(s) From Deep Learning Network Model Trigger RACH Procedure At Network Location Avoid Triggering RACH Procedure At Network Location No Yes 7 Defensive Publications Series, Art."
  },
  {
    "evidence_id": 4,
    "doc_id": "129069349",
    "text": "The UE also records the perceived DL throughput when it connects to a cell with LTE-only connectivity enabled or with EN-DC enabled."
  },
  {
    "evidence_id": 5,
    "doc_id": "129069349",
    "text": "The deep learning model is trained based on the recorded features and labels using, for example, supervised learning."
  },
  {
    "evidence_id": 6,
    "doc_id": "129069349",
    "text": "One cell group provides Fourth Generation (4G) Long-Term Evolution (LTE) access, and the other cell group provides 5G NR access."
  },
  {
    "evidence_id": 7,
    "doc_id": "122371639",
    "text": "4460 [2021] https://www.tdcommons.org/dpubs_series/4460 UE is able to make the best decision to avoid the unnecessary NR RACH procedure."
  },
  {
    "evidence_id": 8,
    "doc_id": "129069349",
    "text": "The UE also records the perceived DL throughput for both the LTE-only mode and the 5G NR dual connectivity mode as labels."
  },
  {
    "evidence_id": 9,
    "doc_id": "129069349",
    "text": "For example, a DL throughput rule may indicate that if the inferred DL throughput of the EN-DC mode is greater than the inferred DL throughput of the LTE-only mode, then the EN-DC mode is to be enabled (or maintained)."
  }
]

